 26:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>2Sa 22:27; Job 9:4; Ps 18:26; Isa 63:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-25","title":"Leviticus 26:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>will bring. De 32:25,41; Jud 2:14-16; Ps 78:62-64; Isa 34:5,6; Jer 9:16 Jer 14:12,13; 15:2-4; La 2:21; Eze 5:17; 6:3; 14:17; 21:4-17; 29:8 Eze 33:2 avenge. De 32:35; Ps 94:1; Eze 20:37; Heb 10:28-30 I will send. Nu 14:12; 16:49; De 28:21; 2Sa 24:15; Jer 14:12; 24:10; 29:17,18 Am 4:10; Lu 21:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-26","title":"Leviticus 26:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>Ps 105:16; Isa 3:1; 9:20; Jer 14:12; La 4:3-9; Eze 4:10,16; 5:16 Eze 14:13; Ho 4:10; Mic 6:14; Hag 1:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-27","title":"Leviticus 26:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>21,24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-28","title":"Leviticus 26:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>in fury. Isa 27:4; 59:18; 63:3; 66:15; Jer 21:5; Eze 5:13,15; 8:18; Na 1:2,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-29","title":"Leviticus 26:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>This was literally fulfilled at the siege of Jerusalem. Josephus gives a dreadful detail respecting a woman named Mary, who, in the extremity of the famine, during the seige, killed her sucking child, roasted, and had eaten part of it, when discovered by the soldiers!</p>\n<p>De 28:53-57; 2Ki 6:28,29; Jer 19:9; La 2:20; 4:10; Eze 5:10 Mt 24:19; Lu 23:29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-30","title":"Leviticus 26:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>I will destroy. 1Ki 13:2; 2Ki 23:8,16,20; 2Ch 14:3-5; 23:17; 31:1; 34:3-7; Isa 27:9 Jer 8:1-3; Eze 6:3-6,13 my soul. 11,15; 20:23; Ps 78:58,59; 89:38; Jer 14:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-31","title":"Leviticus 26:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>And I will make. 2Ki 25:4-10; 2Ch 36:19; Ne 2:3,17; Isa 1:7; 24:10-12; Jer 4:7; 9:11 La 1:1; 2:7; Eze 6:6; 21:15; Mic 3:12 and bring. Ps 74:3-8; Jer 22:5; 26:6,9; 52:13; La 1:10; Eze 9:6; 21:7; 24:21 Mt 24:1,2; Lu 21:5,6,24; Ac 6:14 I will not smell. See on Ge 8:21; Isa 1:11-14; 66:3; Am 5:21-23; Heb 10:26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-32","title":"Leviticus 26:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>And I. De 29:23; Isa 1:7,8; 5:6,9; 6:11; 24:1; 32:13,14; 64:10; Jer 9:11 Jer 25:11,18,38; 44:2,22; La 5:18; Eze 33:28,29; Da 9:2,18 Hab 3:17; Lu 21:20 and your. De 28:37; 29:24-28; 1Ki 9:8; Jer 18:16; 19:8; La 4:12; Eze 5:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-33","title":"Leviticus 26:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>De 4:27; 28:64-66; Ps 44:11; Jer 9:16; La 1:3; 4:15; Eze 12:14-16 Eze 20:23; 22:15; Zec 7:14; Lu 21:24; Jas 1:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-34","title":"Leviticus 26:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>This was fulfilled during the Babylonish captivity: for, from Saul to the captivity are about 490 years, during which period there were 70 sabbaths of years neglected by the Hebrews. Now the Babylonish captivity lasted 70 years, and during that time the land of Israel rested.</p>\n<p>25:2-4,10; 2Ch 36:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-35","title":"Leviticus 26:35","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>Isa 24:5,6; Ro 8:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-36","title":"Leviticus 26:36","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":36,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":36},"content":"<p>I will send. Ge 35:5; De 28:65-67; Jos 2:9-11; 5:1; 1Sa 17:24; 2Ki 7:6,7 2Ch 14:14; Job 15:21,22; Isa 7:2,4; Eze 21:7,12,15 and the. 7,8,17; De 1:44; Job 15:21; Pr 28:1; Isa 30:17 shaken. Heb. driven.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-37","title":"Leviticus 26:37","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":37,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":37},"content":"<p>they shall. Jud 7:22; 1Sa 14:15,16; Isa 10:4; Jer 37:10 and ye shall. Nu 14:42; Jos 7:12,13; Jud 2:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-38","title":"Leviticus 26:38","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":38,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":38},"content":"<p>De 4:27; 28:48,68; Isa 27:13; Jer 42:17,18,22; 44:12-14,27,28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-39","title":"Leviticus 26:39","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":39,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":39},"content":"<p>shall pine. De 28:65; 30:1; Ne 1:9; Ps 32:3,4; Jer 3:25; 29:12; La 4:9; Eze 4:17 Eze 6:9; 20:43; 24:23; 33:10; 36:31; Ho 5:15; Zec 10:9 and also. Ex 20:5; 34:7; Nu 14:18; De 5:9; Jer 31:29; Eze 18:2,3,19 Mt 23:35,36; Ro 11:8-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-40","title":"Leviticus 26:40","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":40,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":40},"content":"<p>confess. Nu 5:7; De 4:29-31; 30:1-3; Jos 7:19; 1Ki 8:33-36,47; Ne 9:2-5 Job 33:27,28; Ps 32:5; Pr 28:13; Jer 31:18-20; Eze 36:31 Da 9:3-20; Ho 5:15; 6:1,2; Lu 15:18,19; 1Jo 1:8-10 and that. 21,24,27,28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-41","title":"Leviticus 26:41","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":41,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":41},"content":"<p>their uncircumcised. De 30:6; Jer 4:4; 6:10; 9:25,26; Eze 44:7; Ac 7:51; Ro 2:28,29 Ga 5:6; Php 3:3; Col 2:11 humbled. Ex 10:3; 1Ki 21:29; 2Ch 12:6,7,12; 32:26; 33:12,13,19,23; Eze 6:9 Eze 20:43; Mt 23:12; Lu 14:11; 18:14; Jas 4:6-9; 1Pe 5:5,6 and they. Ezr 9:13,15; Ne 9:33; Ps 39:9; 51:3,4; Da 9:7-14,18,19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-42","title":"Leviticus 26:42","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":42,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":42},"content":"<p>will I. Ge 9:16; Ex 2:24; 6:5; De 4:31; Ps 106:45; Eze 16:60; Lu 1:72 and I will. Ps 85:1,2; 136:23; Eze 36:1-15,33,34; Joe 2:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-43","title":"Leviticus 26:43","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":43,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":43},"content":"<p>shall enjoy. 34,35 and they. 41; 1Ki 8:46-48; 2Ch 33:12; Job 5:17; 34:31,32; Ps 50:15 Ps 119:67,71,75; Isa 26:16; Jer 31:19; Da 9:7-9,14; Heb 12:5-11 they despised. 15; 2Ki 17:7-17; 2Ch 36:14-16 their soul. 15,30; Ps 50:17; Am 5:10; Zec 11:8; Joh 7:7; 15:23,24; Ro 8:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-44","title":"Leviticus 26:44","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":44,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":44},"content":"<p>I will. De 4:29-31; 2Ki 13:23; Ne 9:31; Ps 94:14; Eze 14:22,23; Ro 11:2,26 abhor. 11 break. Ps 89:33; Jer 14:21; 33:20,21; Eze 16:60</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-45","title":"Leviticus 26:45","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":45,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":45},"content":"<p>for their. Ge 12:2; 15:18; 17:7,8; Ex 2:24; 19:5,6; Lu 1:72,73 Ro 11:12,23-26,28,29; 2Co 3:15,16 whom I. 22:33; 25:38 See on Ex 20:2 in the sight. Ps 98:2,3; Eze 20:9,14,22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lev-26-46","title":"Leviticus 26:46","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LEV","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":46,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":46},"content":"<p>As this verse appears to be the proper concluding verse of the whole book, Dr. A. Clarke thinks that the 27th chapter originally followed the 25th. Others suppose that the 27th chapter was added after the book was finished; and, therefore, there is apparently a double conclusion, one at the end of this, and another at the end of the 27th chapter. All the ancient versions agree in concluding both chapters in nearly the same way.</p>\n<p>the statues. 27:34; De 6:1; 12:1; 13:4; Joh 1:17 in mount Sinai. 25:1 by the hand. 8:36; Nu 4:37; Ps 77:20</p>"}]}